<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch May output seen up 4.3 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch May output seen up 4.3 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect manufacturing production figures for May, due on Thursday, to show a bigger year-on-year increase than in April.</p>
<p>The month-on-month figure for May is expected to rise after a drop in April.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date-Period-Indicator-----------Consensus---Range-----Pvs</p>
<p> 0730 10/7  May  Manufac. output M/M  +1.1 pct   +0.5/+1.7 -2.8</p>
<p> 0730 10/7  May  Manufac. output Y/Y  +4.3 pct   +3.7/+4.9 +3.3</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, J.P. Morgan, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
